    "created_at": "2018-02-02T18:03:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-02T18:03:05Z",
    "body": "In general I don't think breaking out of the web sandbox and running binaries on a user's OS is something we want to allow at all. It drastically breaks the web's security model. Using a cooperating local server, which the user has to install via out-of-band trusted channels, is the canonical way to do this.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
