    "created_at": "2018-02-02T18:16:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-02T18:16:13Z",
    "body": "Fair enough. Suppose was trying to avoid manually opening `terminal` to start the local server; and manually stopping the server when that particular tab or browser instance itself was closed. Possibly using Chromium `--proxy` flag, though uncertain how to tie the browser instance to starting and stopping the local development server, which is more than likely beyond the scope of this issue. \r\n\r\nNot sure if it is possible to somehow use the existing Native Messaging implementation as an underlying process of the present concept - again, without specifically using the Chrome App to achieve the same.\r\n\r\nIn any event, your feedback is helpful.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
