    "created_at": "2018-02-06T17:31:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-06T17:31:19Z",
    "body": "The access to native apps and OS resources been presented in HTML from very beginning. HTA stands for HTML application and was available in IE up to now. Similar approach been considered by other browsers. \r\nThe shell is not something which comes out of the box but with ability to run any executable and trapping std streams by JS, it is not a showstopper. I have used this approach back in 2006 in commercial cross-platform CDs for DOCSIS modem provisioning. Of course there was no unified standard, but was doable. Modern browsers are bit more restrictive and it creates the challenge to make HTML-based native app.\r\n\r\n@annevk , the **type=bash** has sence only in context of HTML application(not as web page). Should this subject be addressed in such context?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
